<h3>Odometer Verification</h3>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Retrieve the Land Rover Bill of Sale (LR bill of lading) document, which contains information about the vehicle including its odometer reading.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the odometer reading on the LR bill of sale to the current mileage displayed on the vehicle's dashboard.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Conduct a visual check of the odometer to ensure it is functioning correctly and displaying accurate mileage.</span></li>
</ul>

<h3>Signed Condition Sign-off</h3>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Review the signed condition report prepared during the pickup process.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the current condition of the vehicle against the documented findings in the signed condition report.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Ask the recipient or authorized person to sign the condition report once they confirm the vehicle meets the agreed-upon conditions.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>Upon completing these steps, the destination delivery handover process is considered complete. If any discrepancies are discovered during the inspection, it is crucial to address them with the seller or shipper before signing off on the condition report and accepting the vehicle.</p>

<p>If the vehicle passes the inspection and all documentation matches the agreed-upon conditions, proceed with signing the condition report:</p>

<ol>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Sign the condition report on behalf of the recipient or authorized person.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Obtain the recipient's or authorized person's signature on the condition report, confirming the vehicle's satisfactory condition.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Ensure the condition report includes the agreed-upon conditions, such as any visible scratches, dents, or damages, and that the vehicle's mileage matches the LR bill of sale.</span></li>
</ol>

<p>Once the signed condition report is obtained, the vehicle is officially accepted, and the recipient or authorized person is responsible for any future claims or issues related to the vehicle's condition.</p>

<p>It is essential to document the inspection process, including photographs and detailed notes, to prove the condition of the vehicle at the time of delivery.</p>

<p>After successfully completing the destination delivery handover, both parties should sign and date the condition report as evidence of the vehicle's condition before acceptance.</p>

<p>If any discrepancies are discovered during the inspection process, it is advisable to address them with the seller or shipper prior to signing the condition report.</p>

<p>By conducting a thorough inspection, ensuring proper documentation, and obtaining both parties' signatures on the condition report, the vehicle delivery process is considered complete, and any potential issues will be addressed before accepting the vehicle.</p></div>
